  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/QjL9jfOUjsu1C1S3E1nM975XyytuoRTxzeDMAma2vxc.original.fullsize.png\"><br />Equation of circle\n$\\mathrm{x}^2+(\\mathrm{y}-(6-\\mathrm{r}))^2=\\mathrm{r}^2$\ntouches $\\sqrt{3} \\mathrm{x}-\\mathrm{y}=0$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{p}=\\mathrm{r} \\\\\n& \\frac{|0-(6-\\mathrm{r})|}{2}=\\mathrm{r} \\\\\n& |\\mathrm{r}-6|=2 \\mathrm{r} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{r}=2\n\\end{aligned}$\n$\\therefore$ Circle $\\mathrm{x}^2+(\\mathrm{y}-4)^2=4$\n$(2,4)$ Satisfies this equation",
